{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"b76296b7fd04aa40b4a7196740e5e41dabc03a7cc3c0c1ae57924dc79be0b8cb","slug":"sections.mcs-projects.cse543-information-assurance-and-security.fuzz-them-all.fuzz-them-all","location":"/Sections/MCS_Projects/CSE543_Information_Assurance_and_Security/Fuzz_Them_All/Fuzz_Them_All.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"CSE543 Information Assurance and Security - Fuzz Them All","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Mark Khusid","given":"Mark","family":"Khusid"},"name":"Mark Khusid","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/markkhusid/MKDynamics_Website_V2","settings":{"output_matplotlib_strings":"remove"},"numbering":{"title":{"offset":3}},"source_url":"https://github.com/markkhusid/MKDynamics_Website_V2/blob/main/Sections/MCS_Projects/CSE543_Information_Assurance_and_Security/Fuzz_Them_All/Fuzz_Them_All.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/markkhusid/MKDynamics_Website_V2/edit/main/Sections/MCS_Projects/CSE543_Information_Assurance_and_Security/Fuzz_Them_All/Fuzz_Them_All.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"Fuzz_Them_All.md","url":"/build/Fuzz_Them_All-fa2ac4b8e199f45dff93e37da69fe094.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Created with Grok Build","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"jb0g3cfn9Q"}],"key":"LxQssP1fx6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The code is a mutational fuzzer in C. It was written in C so the loop would be fast. A seed is copied into a working buffer. Each iteration may replace a byte. Every 500 iterations, ten more bytes are appended. The buffer is then written out for a separate runner.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"dE5asoanWH"}],"key":"BP91mH5uEh"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The runner and the course programs it fed stay off this page. The novelty is the mutator itself.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"VrqwEng3GO"}],"key":"NnCMpJWwzm"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"One byte at a time, 13 percent of the time","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"KemAKqQRfW"}],"identifier":"one-byte-at-a-time-13-percent-of-the-time","label":"One byte at a time, 13 percent of the time","html_id":"one-byte-at-a-time-13-percent-of-the-time","implicit":true,"key":"yVJwoAWhP0"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For each byte, the fuzzer draws a number from 0 to 100. If that draw is 13 or less, the byte is replaced with a random value from 1 to 255. The identifier in the submission says “13 percent.” The test is ","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"pb1GRFq5zq"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<= 13","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"lgD7kS4ZDg"},{"type":"text","value":" on a draw of ","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"ZioM2nnDfI"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rand() % 101","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"vZl8e3fc5G"},{"type":"text","value":", so the rate is a little higher than 13 percent. That off-by-one is part of what the code actually does.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"U5e8H52Ubn"}],"key":"tFRq769sBp"},{"type":"code","lang":"c","value":"void mutate_buffer(char *buf, int size)\n{\n    int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        if ((rand() % 101) <= 13) {\n            buf[i] = (char)((rand() % 255) + 1);\n        }\n    }\n}","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"key":"fmuVFqBFNH"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Zero is never written. A mutated byte is always in 1..255, so a C string inside the buffer is less likely to end early on a fresh zero. That choice matters when the target treats the buffer as a string.","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"aplKE1NL2l"}],"key":"Wvl7fDBMHw"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Growing the input","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"wswrtwFmbf"}],"identifier":"growing-the-input","label":"Growing the input","html_id":"growing-the-input","implicit":true,"key":"blx5N72Gsg"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every 500th iteration appends ten new random bytes and returns the new length. A fixed seed can only reach bugs near the front of the input. Growing the buffer is how the same seed eventually reaches a bug that depends on length.","position":{"start":{"line":30,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"key":"LhddhivklK"}],"key":"VPTBhzNEbU"},{"type":"code","lang":"c","value":"int add_10_random_bytes(char *buf, int size)\n{\n    int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n        buf[size + i] = (char)((rand() % 255) + 1);\n    }\n    return size + 10;\n}","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"NlsvzhN3o1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main loop is those two calls. Mutate on every iteration. Grow when the iteration count is a multiple of 500. After the last iteration, write the buffer to stdout.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"T1BDicXLwb"}],"key":"vn5kHYM72T"}],"key":"cRfLAyLE2l"}],"key":"NfgHlEh35g"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"CSE543 Information Assurance and Security - UDP Spoofing","url":"/sections/mcs-projects/cse543-information-assurance-and-security/udp-spoofing/udp-spoofing","group":"Master's in Computer Science (Cybersecurity) Projects"},"next":{"title":"CSE543 Information Assurance and Security - Fuzzer Project","url":"/sections/mcs-projects/cse543-information-assurance-and-security/fuzzer-project/fuzzer-project","group":"Master's in Computer Science (Cybersecurity) Projects"}}},"domain":"https://www.mkdynamics.net"}